WEBVTT

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.940
CARRIER PIGEON

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:48.520
He's going to kick us out.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:49.940
Like hell he is!

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.400
What the...?

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:55.740
I upgraded to a new model!
How d'you like it?

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.200
Let's go, Satoru!

00:01:58.990 --> 00:01:59.820
Shit!

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.240
I've gotta hide!

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:05.580
But where?

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:10.790
Nobu, is that you?

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.590
I'm sorry, Nobu had an accident.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:15.510
Please open the door.

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:16.970
So this is it?

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.220
Your little hidey hole.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:23.060
We're going to change
your memories, Hiroki.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:24.220
Tsukasa?

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.930
Consider this payback
for crushing Mr. Hayashi.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.690
I didn't... I wouldn't!

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.480
Then who did?

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:36.860
Who else could possibly crush
Mr. Hayashi, other than you?

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:37.990
Tell me, Hiroki.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:41.950
Why are you doing this, Tsukasa?
You know I can't say the truth.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.990
Do you really think you can beat me?

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.620
Not yet, Satoru. First I need
to take him to my peak.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.250
Did you have no choice
but to blame me?

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.630
-Even so, this is too cruel!
-In there, he'll be unable to fight back.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.260
Because my peak has a very strong lock.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:58.670
This is too much...

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.050
It's okay.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:05.140
It's our back door trick, Hiroki.
I'm going to crush Satoru.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.390
Keep still now!

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.270
Crush Satoru?

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:11.440
Go on Satoru, you're up.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.020
Is that what all this is about?!

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:17.280
Hiroki!

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.650
You're going nowhere!

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.030
Crap!

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.370
What was that?

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:31.580
It's just Boo...

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:37.090
I gotta... run away.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:38.090
What happened?

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:42.300
He escaped by letting his own image
get cut in half.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.590
That crazy bastard...

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:51.480
Mr. Katsuragi, Hiroki is in that apartment
behind the convenience store.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:54.150
We have to get him, fast...

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:56.480
Dammit Hiroki... Don't you get it?

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:58.900
I gotta move.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.360
Nobu, you answer it.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.740
Who the hell is it?

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.740
Delivery.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:12.370
-Yeah, I'm coming. Hold your horses.-Gotta run.

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:17.420
Gotta run away...

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:20.010
Nobu?

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:27.600
You stupid or something?
You can't run away from us.

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:37.310
Careful, he's covered in puke.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:38.770
No wonder he's out of it.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:43.360
That trick he used was like tearing off
your own arm to wake yourself up.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:46.410
Why don't we finish the job
before he comes around?

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:47.870
Let's leave it till tomorrow.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.080
I can't do any more today.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:52.910
Tsukasa's not slept at all.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:56.290
I can do it by myself if necessary.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:59.880
It'd be too dangerous
to let you do it alone.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:02.380
I'd be fine.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:04.010
You guys hungry?

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.180
Sure. Sounds good. Tsukasa?

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:10.560
I'm good. I'm going to
have a rest in the back.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:14.940
I think we'd better do it tomorrow,
seeing how he's this tired.

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:19.060
You know, right?

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.070
Hiroki's figured out that
you crushed Hayashi.

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:27.570
You'd better change his memories
before Satoru gets suspicious.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.700
It's your neck on the line here.

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:32.160
I know that much, Long.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:35.080
I'm tired. Let me rest first.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:41.880
I need to get Hiroki on board tonight.

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:44.340
He doesn't understand
the situation at all.

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:48.180
This is our last chance.

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:51.470
Erm, where is Mr. Hayashi?

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:55.850
We took him to the hospital.
We thought it'd be less stressful for him.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:59.020
You could have put him in my room...

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:00.440
You kidding?!

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.940
Having that vegetable here
gave me the creeps!

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:05.440
I don't want him around.

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:07.450
I've lost my appetite!

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:09.070
I'm going back to my room.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:12.870
Satoru! Wait!

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:14.830
How can he talk about him like that?

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:18.620
He worked with Mr. Hayashi for years...

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:23.210
Why's he always like that, anyway?
I've had enough of taking his crap.

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:26.260
You're right.
I'm sorry you had to hear that.

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:32.260
It's not your fault.
You shouldn't have to apologize.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:36.470
It's not hard to see why you and Katsuragi
don't see eye to eye.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:38.850
He doesn't get on with anyone,
not just me.

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:45.230
I didn't mean it like that. Your door is
from that anime about a robot cat, right?

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:46.860
That's why.

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:47.860
What do you mean?

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:51.490
You know Katsuragi hates cats, right?

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:54.620
Really? I didn't actually...

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:57.750
The "bigeon" hates cats!

00:06:59.040 --> 00:06:59.620
What...?

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.540
I'll have your food
brought to your room, okay?

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:06.130
-Why did Meiling come to mind?
-Or shall we eat together, here?

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:09.130
Mister said to tell you
there's a "carry-a-bigeon".

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:13.350
Hang on! If the cat-hating "bigeon"
is a carrier pigeon, then maybe...

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:14.890
What do you say, Satoru?

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:18.140
Dinner. Do you want to eat with me?

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:19.520
I... err...

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:23.690
I'm over-thinking it. Why would
Katsuragi be a carrier pigeon?

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:26.190
What do you think you're doing?

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.820
Katsuragi. Have you
finished eating already?

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:34.530
No, I have not. This idiot went downstairs
without even taking the key to the room.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:40.500
I'll have my food in the room with
this dolt. You can eat upstairs.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.290
-Hey, Katsuragi...
-It's fine, Jin.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.340
I'm not mad anymore.

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:48.630
You sure? Okay then.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:53.430
I mean... it couldn't hurt
to test out my theory.

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:59.560
If he's Mr. Hayashi's carrier pigeon,
there's only one keyword possible.

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:04.310
Mr. Katsuragi, do you know
a guy called Mr. Matasa?

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:09.610
Err...

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:15.200
Is he here?

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:19.790
Is Mr. Matasa here?

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.660
Where is he? I have...

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:23.210
He's a carrier pigeon!

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:25.670
I have to see him. It's very important.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.500
But... why?

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:31.420
-I have something for him...
-I am Mr. Matasa.

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:32.720
You?

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:36.140
Yes. I'm keeping it secret
from the others.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:39.310
But in fact, I am Mr. Matasa.

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:45.770
You're serious?
You'll take it somewhere safe, then?

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:49.480
The room's bugged so keep it down
when we get inside.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:53.030
What the hell is going on?

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:56.410
It would've been a disaster
if someone had found it.

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:58.280
But...

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:03.960
I don't have to worry anymore.
Here. You'll take it, right?

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:05.330
Sure.

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:10.710
Mr. Hayashi must have
given this to Katsuragi.

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:25.890
What the hell is on this thing anyway?

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:29.980
Forgive me, Satoru.

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:34.440
This was the only way to contact you
without putting you in danger.

00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:37.910
This is important.
Don't trust anything the Company says!

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:41.950
That's not all, Satoru.
You need to escape from the Company.

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:44.080
Escape?

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.960
What... What is going on?!

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:54.800
Satoru, you need to escape
from the Company.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:58.840
If you're reading this, that means you
 have already met Meiling.

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:01.970
I had to make that child without a lock

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:04.850
because the Company was holding you
as a hostage.

00:10:05.890 --> 00:10:08.850
There is one other person
with whom I shared my peak.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:11.520
His name is Tsukasa.

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:15.320
He was taken from me when
you and I began living together.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:18.360
Everything started from there.

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:23.280
All of it. It all happened
because I found you...

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:28.000
Tsukasa. I'm home.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.540
We've moved Tsukasa to a hotel.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:35.710
It seems I'll be looking after him
from now on.

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:37.510
What're you talking about?

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.930
The CEO's orders, I'm afraid.

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:41.760
Impossible.

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:49.140
We can't have all the ability users
living together under one roof.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:54.150
We tried that with the qigong masters,
and what happened then?

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:56.780
They killed my father.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:57.780
But that's not...

00:10:57.940 --> 00:11:01.610
I want guarantees that we can feel safe.

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:03.530
This is no less than kidnapping!

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:09.250
All I want is for Tsukasa
to grow up to be like you,

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:13.420
an adult who does the Company's bidding
without grumbling.

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:16.170
I have no intention of making
Tsukasa do Company work.

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:18.170
Return Tsukasa to my care!

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:20.130
Listen, Hayashi.

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:24.180
That kid was originally bought so we could
sell his organs, remember?

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:27.430
We gave him to you because
you seemed to want him.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:34.440
I'd first met Tsukasa
a while after that terrible incident.

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:39.110
Because of me, all of the qigong masters
had been murdered.

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:40.820
At such a time...

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:47.200
it was Tsukasa's smile that relieved me
of the guilt I'd been carrying.

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:51.080
Your sneakers are
completely soaked now, Tsukasa.

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:53.630
But it's just so amazing!

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:56.340
To think that all of this...

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:59.380
All of it has come flowing in
from so far out.

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:02.970
What you said was true, Mr. Hayashi!

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:07.970
I can't believe I made it here.

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:11.890
If anything happens to Tsukasa,

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:13.730
I won't forgive you.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:19.360
I won't do anything to the boy,
but you might.

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:22.360
If anything ever happens to Tsukasa,

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:25.740
the blame will be yours
and yours alone.

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:28.740
Let me see him one more time.

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:31.790
Very well.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:36.790
We need to do as the Company says
in order to survive.

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:40.170
You'll be safe so long as
you work for them, okay?

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:46.010
Twelve years have passed since that day,
and I'm still concerned for Tsukasa.

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:50.520
In truth, I wish you would take him
with you and run away.

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:54.440
Or at least just come with Meiling...

00:12:55.270 --> 00:12:59.270
But the most important thing for me
is that you make it out of there.

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:01.280
Mr. Hayashi...

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:05.780
never suspected for one moment
that he would be crushed.

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:09.530
Even if I did run away,
Mr. Hayashi's gone now.

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.290
Just what the hell do I do?

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:15.670
I want you to be careful before
you go speaking with Tsukasa.

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:21.380
There is an ability user named Hiroki,
with whom Tsukasa shared his peak.

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:26.090
If you are to escape with Tsukasa,
you must bring Hiroki too.

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:29.260
Otherwise he might well
be kidnapped by the Company.

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:33.180
What are you talking about?
You were crushed by Hiroki!

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:36.940
He crushed you because you made Meiling.

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:40.270
Wait... that's weird.

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:42.610
As soon as Hiroki spoke to Mr. Hayashi,

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:44.990
he'd realize it was a misunderstanding.

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:48.070
Mr. Hayashi never wanted
to make Meiling after all.

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:51.200
I'm planning not to give Meiling a lock.

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.580
What was that memory all about then?

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:58.080
Could it have been altered by someone?

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:00.210
But Satoru...

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:03.590
I want you to be extra careful
around Tsukasa.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:04.760
What?

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:10.260
The Company told me unless I made Meiling,
they'd have Tsukasa crush me.

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:15.600
If Tsukasa truly has been brainwashed
to the point of being able to do that,

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:19.350
talking to him about escaping
could put your life at risk.

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:23.440
That's why I first want you
to sound out his opinion on Meiling.

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:26.860
If you find out that he agrees
with how she was made,

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:29.360
you can assume he is
on the Company's side.

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:34.910
What did you do to Meiling?

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:37.620
We were testing her out
with a Company employee,

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:39.750
but it seems he's opened a can of worms.

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:43.750
I didn't realize they were alive!
Or I wouldn't have started the fire!

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:57.390
Look at the butterfly, Meiling.

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:00.100
Look at your butterfly.

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:05.730
This is a disaster.
Look at her peak!

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:09.950
If you make her work like this,
it'll soon destroy her!

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:13.280
I guess we'll just have to find
a new "baby" before then.

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:15.450
And you think I'd let you do that?

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:20.330
You have no say in this. So shut up
and share your peak when we tell you.

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:25.420
The cruelty of not allowing someone
a lock would be clear

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:29.470
to anyone who understood
the importance of a person's peak.

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:32.680
But at the same time,
only someone familiar

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:35.680
with how images work
could have come up with this idea.

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:40.060
I don't want to believe it,
but Tsukasa could be helping them.

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:43.770
Even if he really has been turned
by the Company,

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:47.570
there may still be a solution
to all this.

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:50.990
When I was in Beijing,
something happened that meant

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.530
I had no choice but to hide
Mr. Katsuragi's memories.

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:55.160
Hide them?

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:59.700
You must make sure the Company
never finds out about this technique.

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:04.540
Because, in fact, I told the CEO
I had removed Mr. Katsuragi's memories

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:06.880
when actually I just hid them.

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:09.590
I'll prepare a separate note
on the method itself.

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:12.340
But if you detect the slightest danger,

00:16:12.590 --> 00:16:16.220
I want you to drop this idea
and just find a way to escape.

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:20.020
Satoru, make sure you get out of there.

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:22.310
I want to start over.

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:27.730
On that unfortunate day
12 years ago, I found you.

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:33.490
Thinking I might be able to help you
was a mistake I can never rectify.

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:36.490
You're wrong. It wasn't a mistake.

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:39.660
I owe everything to you...

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:45.500
Because of my mistake, all of your lives
were thrown into disarray.

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:48.170
That's why...

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:51.300
I intend to take you all back
from the Company's clutches.

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:53.630
Every one of you...

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:56.840
Starting with you, Satoru.

00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:59.010
Follow the map.

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:03.230
You'll find me waiting
for you at the endpoint.

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:07.860
Dammit.

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:19.030
Are you all right, Hiroki?

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:23.290
Why do you get in the way like that?

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:27.460
Why won't you listen to what I say?

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:31.300
Do you really want to be
ripped away from me?

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:36.630
Please, don't leave me
on my own any longer.

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:40.600
Why did things end up like this...?

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:44.730
Tsukasa and I both just
want to be together.

00:17:45.940 --> 00:17:48.650
I'm sorry, Tsukasa.

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:51.020
I promise I'm not going anywhere.

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:54.530
I'll stay by your side forever, okay?

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:56.320
Hiroki...

00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:58.910
Hey!

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:03.080
Are you dimwits drinking on the job?
Do you want to get the sack?!

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:07.000
Are you asleep?

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:09.080
What's the commotion? It's late.

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:13.590
Nothing. Satoru said he wanted
to check on Hiroki.

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:15.720
I just went to look myself.

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:17.300
He's asleep.

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:20.510
These guys insisted I ask Long
before opening this door,

00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:23.600
but I can't go waking him up constantly.

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:26.600
Don't worry, Satoru. Go get some rest.

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:30.230
I'll go to bed soon too,
after I've looked in on Mr. Hayashi.

00:18:30.650 --> 00:18:33.730
You haven't heard? Mr. Hayashi isn't here.

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:34.940
What?

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:36.740
They moved him to the hospital.

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:41.240
Shit.

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:44.040
Who told them they could just...?

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:57.260
Was Hiroki really the one
who crushed Mr. Hayashi?

00:18:58.130 --> 00:18:59.340
What're you saying?

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:01.220
Do you have any proof?

00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:04.140
This can't be. Has he
sensed something is up?

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:05.140
Proof?

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:09.890
Hiroki was against Mr. Hayashi
creating Meiling, so...

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:12.150
And what do you think of Meiling?

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:15.730
I can't say I think it's
an ideal way of doing things.

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:18.780
But... if those were Mr. Hayashi's wishes,

00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:20.530
then I intend to fulfill them.

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:25.660
I would likely say the same thing
if I believed Mr. Katsuragi's memories.

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:27.620
So...

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:31.210
you're saying you didn't actually
see Hiroki crush Mr. Hayashi?

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:35.710
Of course not! I'd have crushed Hiroki
to stop him if I'd been there!

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:40.590
Right... It makes sense that Tsukasa
can't stay cool over this matter.

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:44.180
That would make him
extremely easy to manipulate.

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:47.390
What are you trying to say here, Satoru?

00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:51.190
If Tsukasa harbored any resentment
against Mr. Hayashi,

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:53.400
he wouldn't have cried like that.

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:58.980
It is possible that Mr. Katsuragi's
memories have been fabricated.

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:02.910
Long could have changed them
by using Meiling.

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:05.700
We may have been duped.

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:09.370
Perfect. It's Long he suspects!

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:11.370
We've been duped?

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:14.330
So you're saying that
Long crushed Mr. Hayashi?

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:17.840
He couldn't have,
but he might have drugged him!

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:21.090
This is perfect, Satoru.
You really are a good little idiot.

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:24.720
In that case, why didn't Hiroki
say he was innocent?

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:27.430
There might be a reason.

00:20:28.010 --> 00:20:33.480
Even Mr. Hayashi couldn't tell us anything
because you were being held hostage.

00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:37.900
The Company's methods are saved on this.

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:40.820
Mr. Hayashi typed it all up
before he was crushed.

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:45.700
He describes how you were kidnapped
in exchange for me,

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:49.200
and how he had to do whatever
the Company said because of that.

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:51.000
What is he talking about?

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:55.000
Mr. Hayashi wanted us
to get away from the Company.

00:20:55.670 --> 00:21:00.380
But he was also worried you might
have been brainwashed by them...

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:04.340
Mr. Hayashi worried more about you
than about anyone else.

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:06.680
Tsukasa... we can escape, can't we?

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:08.850
He was worried?

00:21:09.010 --> 00:21:10.140
Why?

00:21:11.060 --> 00:21:13.560
Why would Mr. Hayashi...?

00:21:14.190 --> 00:21:17.810
What are you doing, Tsukasa?
 Get out of here, now!

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:21.650
Stop this, Tsukasa!
 You'll be crushed too!

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:23.740
Why...

00:21:23.990 --> 00:21:26.320
are you worrying about me?

00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:28.200
Tsukasa.

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:32.040
There's no way I would ever
forget about you.

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:40.710
Why?

00:21:40.960 --> 00:21:43.550
Why?

00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:46.510
Why did I crush him...?

00:21:47.050 --> 00:21:48.430
Are you okay?

00:21:50.100 --> 00:21:51.640
Satoru...

00:21:52.220 --> 00:21:54.270
Where am I supposed to run to?

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:57.100
Mr. Hayashi has plotted out
an escape route.

00:21:57.350 --> 00:21:58.650
That's not what I mean!

00:21:59.060 --> 00:22:03.110
Where the hell can I ever run to?!

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:04.940
What's the ruckus?

00:22:06.360 --> 00:22:09.820
Satoru has picked up
a message from Hayashi.

00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:12.910
He's planning to run away
from the Company.

00:22:13.370 --> 00:22:15.660
Shoot him before he tries to escape!

00:22:16.040 --> 00:22:17.410
Stop right there, Satoru!

00:23:50.130 --> 00:23:55.050
Artist: Tomoko Ninomiya
